# s_in takes a number (B13), and p_i takes only @, like any niladic
# function: a value is a type error, never ignored (rule 7).
== SOURCE
s_in "a"
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected a number, found Char
 --> -e:1:1
  |
1 | s_in "a"
  | ^^^^^^^^
  |      --- a string: a vector of Char
  = note: `s_in` has type Num a => a -> Float
  = help: a string is text, not a number: write a number without quotes
